1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,500
ProofOfPost - on-chain content-rule adjudication

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:05,120
What if content rules could be enforced on-chain?

3
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:07,920
Post content, define natural-language rules, back it with a GEN bond.

4
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:11,840
Connect a studio-dev-only signer - the key stays in memory.

5
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:17,040
Submit content and define the rules it must satisfy.

6
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:22,220
submit() locks the 1 GEN bond and creates a PENDING entry.

7
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:26,340
The write settles through validator consensus… (sped up 16x)

8
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:31,420
FINALIZED - entry #2 sits in the registry as PENDING.

9
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:35,940
evaluate() asks the validators to judge the content.

10
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:40,960
Each validator independently re-derives the verdict. (sped up 20x)

11
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:44,320
Settled verdict: COMPLIANT - all three rules satisfied.

12
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:48,020
The contract refunds the bond to the submitter.

13
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,900
appeal() re-opens consensus on a NON_COMPLIANT verdict (max 2).

14
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:56,980
Appeal consensus… (sped up 24x)

15
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:02,400
Verdict stands: NON_COMPLIANT, appeals 1 - bond stays slashed.

16
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:05,100
ProofOfPost explores verifiable content compliance with intelligent contracts.
